  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Mid Term Evaluation AGIR II</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Mid Term Evaluation AGIR II</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Sveriges ambassad i Maputo st&#xf6;djer sedan  2014 ett  program f&#xf6;r st&#xf6;d till civila samh&#xe4;lle i Mocambique under namnet AGIR II. Programmet &#xe4;r en samfinansiering mellan Sverige, Holland och Denmark. Programmet implementeras av 4 internationella NGOs, (Oxfam Ibis, Oxfam Novib, Diakonia och We Effect) som kallas IPO (Intermediary partner organisation) . Den totala budgeten f&#xf6;r AGIR II under de 3 &#xe5;r som ska utv&#xe4;rderas &#xe4;r 442.886 800 SEK.Sverige har bidragit med 361 929 495 SEK,  Holland med 52 260 615 (delegated partnership)  SEK, och Danmark med 28 696 690 SEK (delegated partnership))

St&#xf6;det till AGIR II regleras av avtal mellan Sverige och  varje IPO. I art 6.6 i avtalet f&#xf6;reskrivs det att Sverige separat kommer att upphandla en oberoende halvtidsutv&#xe4;rdering f&#xf6;r att f&#xf6;lja upp utvecklingen av alla komponenter i AGIR II. Detta beslut g&#xe4;ller upphandling av en s&#xe5;dan halvtidsutv&#xe4;rdering som kommer att omfatta verksamhetsperioden 1 december 2014 -31 december 2017.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The purpose or intended use of the evaluation is:
&#x2022;To help the donors (The Embassies of Sweden, Denmark and the Netherlands) and their partners (Oxfam IBIS, Oxfam Novib, Diakonia and We Effect) to assess progress of the on-going programme AGIR II to learn from what works well and less well to inform decisions on how project implementation may be adjusted and improved. Furthermore, the purpose is to provide the donors and their partners with an input to upcoming discussions concerning the preparation of a possible new phase of the AGIR pogramme.
&#x2022;To advise on changes needed in the program guidelines and in the general functioning of the program.
The evaluation object is the AGIR II programme December 2014- December 2020. The time to be evaluated is December 2014- December 2017</narrative>
  </description>
